---
import Layout from './_layouts/Layout.astro';
import CallToActionBlock from '~/components/blocks/composite/CallToAction.astro';
import ContentCarouselBlock from '~/components/blocks/composite/ContentCarousel.astro';
import TabsBlock from '~/components/blocks/composite/Tabs.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: {
    default: 'Composing blocks',
  },
};

const slides = [
  {
    src: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?w=800&h=600&fit=crop',
    alt: 'Mountain landscape',
  },
  {
    src: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469474968028-56623f02e42e?w=800&h=600&fit=crop',
    alt: 'Forest path',
  },
];

const presenceExample = `<CallToAction headline={{ title: 'No actions' }} />

<CallToAction
  headline={{ title: 'With actions' }}
  actions={[{ label: 'Get started' }]}
/>

<ContentCarousel items={slides} prevButton={false} nextButton={false} />`;

const layersExample = `<Tabs
  items={[{ label: 'Overview' }, { label: 'API' }, { label: 'Examples' }]}
  defaultItemConfig={{ variant: 'ghost', intent: 'neutral' }}
  activeItemConfig={{ variant: 'solid', intent: 'primary' }}
/>`;

const orderExample = `<Tabs
  items={[{ label: 'Overview' }, { label: 'Pinned', class: 'underline' }]}
  defaultItemConfig={{ variant: 'ghost', intent: 'neutral' }}
  activeItemConfig={{ variant: 'solid', intent: 'primary' }}
/>`;

const classesExample = `<CallToAction
  headline={{ title: 'Flat card' }}
  container={{ content: { class: 'shadow-none rounded-none' } }}
/>`;
---

<Layout
  metadata={metadata}
  headline={{
    tagline: 'Guide',
    title: 'Composing blocks',
    subtitle: 'How every block exposes its children, and how your config reaches them.',
  }}
>
  <p>
    Blocks are built from other blocks. A Header holds buttons, a Tabs block holds a row of tab
    buttons, a CallToAction holds a headline and actions. Every block exposes those children the
    same way, so once you know the pattern you can configure any of them.
  </p>
  <p>
    A prop with no suffix configures <strong>one child</strong> (<code>closeButton</code>,
    <code>headline</code>) or a list of them (<code>actions</code>, <code>items</code>). A prop
    ending in <code>Config</code> is a <strong>layer</strong>: settings merged into many children at
    once (<code>defaultItemConfig</code>, <code>activeItemConfig</code>). The API reference on each
    block's page links both kinds to the child block's own props.
  </p>

  <h2>Turning children on and off</h2>
  <p>
    An optional child renders when you set its prop, and not otherwise. There are no
    <code>show…</code> switches. A child that renders by default is hidden by passing
    <code>false</code>.
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-surface p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm border border-border"><code>{presenceExample}</code></pre>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 my-6" data-doc-section="presence">
    <div data-doc-example="no-actions">
      <CallToActionBlock headline={{ title: 'No actions', htmlTag: 'h3' }} />
    </div>
    <div data-doc-example="with-actions">
      <CallToActionBlock
        headline={{ title: 'With actions', htmlTag: 'h3' }}
        actions={[{ label: 'Get started' }]}
      />
    </div>
    <div class="border border-border rounded-lg overflow-hidden" data-doc-example="no-arrows">
      <ContentCarouselBlock items={slides} prevButton={false} nextButton={false} />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Styling many children at once</h2>
  <p>
    A <code>default…Config</code> layer applies to every child in the list, in every state. A state
    layer such as <code>activeItemConfig</code>, <code>selectedItemConfig</code> or
    <code>highlightedTierConfig</code> sits on top of it and applies only while the child is in that
    state. Set the shared look once, then only what changes.
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-surface p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm border border-border"><code>{layersExample}</code></pre>
  <div class="my-6" data-doc-section="layers">
    <TabsBlock
      items={[{ label: 'Overview' }, { label: 'API' }, { label: 'Examples' }]}
      defaultItemConfig={{ variant: 'ghost', intent: 'neutral' }}
      activeItemConfig={{ variant: 'solid', intent: 'primary' }}
    >
      <p slot="panel-0">Overview panel.</p>
      <p slot="panel-1">API panel.</p>
      <p slot="panel-2">Examples panel.</p>
    </TabsBlock>
  </div>

  <h2>Who wins</h2>
  <p>Each child is built from these layers, later ones overriding earlier ones:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>the block's own internal defaults;</li>
    <li>
      the <code>default…Config</code> layer;
    </li>
    <li>the state layer, while the child is in that state;</li>
    <li>
      the child's own entry (<code>items[n]</code>, <code>closeButton</code>, …).
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The child's own entry always wins, so anything you set on it applies in every state. To style a
    child only while it is active or selected, use the state layer instead. Below, the second tab's
    <code>underline</code> stays whether it is active or not.
  </p>
  <p>
    Settings that identify a single element, such as <code>id</code>, <code>name</code> and
    <code>anchorId</code>, can't go in a layer. Set them on the child's own entry.
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-surface p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm border border-border"><code>{orderExample}</code></pre>
  <div class="my-6" data-doc-section="order">
    <TabsBlock
      items={[{ label: 'Overview' }, { label: 'Pinned', class: 'underline' }]}
      defaultItemConfig={{ variant: 'ghost', intent: 'neutral' }}
      activeItemConfig={{ variant: 'solid', intent: 'primary' }}
    >
      <p slot="panel-0">Overview panel.</p>
      <p slot="panel-1">Pinned panel.</p>
    </TabsBlock>
  </div>

  <h2>Overriding classes</h2>
  <p>
    Classes you pass are added to a block's defaults, never swapped for them. When your class and a
    default belong to the same group, yours wins: <code>shadow-none</code> removes a default
    <code>shadow-xl</code>, <code>rounded-none</code> removes a default <code>rounded-md</code>. Use
    the opposite utility to cancel a default; you never need <code>!</code>.
  </p>
  <pre class="bg-surface p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm border border-border"><code>{classesExample}</code></pre>
  <div class="my-6" data-doc-section="classes">
    <CallToActionBlock
      headline={{ title: 'Flat card', htmlTag: 'h3' }}
      container={{ content: { class: 'shadow-none rounded-none' } }}
    />
  </div>
</Layout>
